title: "Get a webhook destination"
icon: arrow-down-left
description: "Get a webhook destination: getWebhookDestination in the TypeScript, Python and Rust clients."
---

`GET /v1/projects/{projectId}/webhooks/destinations/{destinationId}`

Returns the configuration of one webhook destination belonging to the selected project. Missing or deleted destinations are reported as errors. This read does not disclose the signing secret returned when the destination or a secret rotation was created.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.projects.getWebhookDestination(input: GetWebhookDestinationInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<GetWebhookDestinationOutput>
```
</Tab>
